export const TAXPRACTICE_KB = "# TaxPractice Support Knowledge Base\n\nSupport handbook for tickets about the TaxPractice training simulator and its return checker: who can do what, how each feature works, the exact error messages people see, and the fix for each.\n\n- App: TaxPractice (Tax Practice Simulator)\n- Sign-in: tax-practice-simulator-l5mh.vercel.app\n- Owner: Higher View Legacies (administrator)\n- Tax year: 2025 forms\n\n## What the app is\n\nTaxPractice is a **training simulator for tax preparers**. It generates fully fictional client scenarios — a taxpayer, every supporting document (W-2, 1099s, Schedule C worksheet, 1098-T and more), preparer tasks and a line-by-line answer key — so preparers can practise entering returns without touching real taxpayer data.\n\n- Every person, employer and identifier in a scenario is fictional. Every generated page is watermarked **TRAINING SAMPLE — NOT FOR FILING**.\n- All numbers and the answer key come from a tested tax calculator, never from AI. AI only helps describe a scenario.\n- The forms and answer keys are for tax year **2025**.\n\n**What it is not.** It is not filing software. It does not e-file, does not prepare real returns, and does not connect to any tax software or client records.\n\nOne feature handles real documents: the Return checker, for office and admin accounts. It checks a return someone already prepared, entirely inside the user's browser.\n\n## Account types and what each can do\n\nEvery login belongs to one of three types. The header shows it after sign-in: the office name and role (for example \"Smile Tax Services · office\"), or \"Administrator\".\n\n| Can they… | Admin | Office | Preparer |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| See their office's scenarios + built-in scenarios | All offices | Yes | Yes |\n| Generate new scenarios | Yes (become built-in) | Yes (for their office) | No |\n| Save scenarios | Automatic | Save button | No |\n| Delete scenarios | Any | Their office's only | No |\n| See the answer key | Always | Always | After all preparer tasks are ticked |\n| Download documents as PDF | Yes | No | No |\n| Use the scenario assistant (AI) | Yes | Yes | No |\n| Return checker (real returns) | Yes | Yes | No |\n| Scan & organize (training documents) | Yes | Yes | Yes |\n| Team page (preparer link) | — | Yes | No |\n| Admin page (offices, logins, passwords) | Yes | No | No |\n\n- **Admin** belongs to no office and manages everything.\n- **Office** is the office owner's login (one office can have more than one office login).\n- **Preparer** is the office's trainees. All preparers of an office share one login, opened through the office's preparer link.\n\nPages a role can't use are hidden; if someone types the address anyway, they are sent back to Scenarios, and the server refuses the action with \"Your account can't do that.\"\n\n## Signing in\n\n### Office and admin accounts\n\n1. Open the site. Every page sends you to **Sign in**.\n2. Enter the email and password the administrator gave you. Press **Continue**.\n\n### Preparers\n\n1. Open the link the office sent (it looks like …vercel.app/login/<long code>).\n2. Enter only the password the office gave with the link. The page says **Preparer sign-in**.\n\n### Things that are by design\n\n- **No sign-up.** Only the administrator creates office logins; offices create the preparer link.\n- **No \"forgot password\".** Office passwords are reset only by the administrator (Admin page → Reset password). The preparer link password is changed by the office on its Team page.\n- **No welcome email from the app.** Logins and links are sent to people separately (by the administrator's own messaging).\n- **No \"Sign in with Google\" in this app.** A few logins also belong to the owner's other app (Referral Circle). Those people sign in here with their Referral Circle email and that app's password; if they only ever used Google there, the administrator sets a password for them.\n- **Staying signed in.** Sessions persist in the browser until **Sign out** (top right).\n\n## Scenarios\n\nA scenario is one fictional client: household, income, every document, preparer tasks and an answer key. The **Scenarios** page lists two groups.\n\n| Group | Who made it | Who sees it | Who can delete it |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **[Office name] scenarios** | That office's office account | Only that office (office + its preparers) | That office, or the admin |\n| **Built-in scenarios** | The admin (plus the bundled demos) | Every office and preparer | The admin only (bundled demos can't be deleted) |\n\n### Generating a scenario (office and admin)\n\n1. Click **New scenario**. Pick a template (Beginner → Expert), describe the client, or talk it through with the assistant, then fine-tune.\n2. Click **Generate scenario**. If it says **Loading your account…**, wait a second; it enables itself.\n3. **Office:** the scenario opens with a **Not saved yet** notice and an **Unsaved** badge in the list. Click **Save scenario** so the office and its preparers can open it. Unsaved scenarios are gone after a reload, and the browser warns before leaving the page.\n4. **Admin:** the scenario is saved straight into the built-in scenarios for everyone.\n\n### Other actions\n\n- **Generate a variant** — same setup, different fictional people and numbers.\n- **Seed** — the scenario's code; the same setup and seed always produce exactly the same scenario.\n- **Delete** — asks to confirm, then returns to the list. It can't be undone.\n- No two scenarios share a fictional person or SSN.\n\n## Scenario tabs\n\nOpening a scenario shows these tabs, in this order.\n\n| Tab | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Documents** | Every document as a watermarked page preview. Admins also get Download PDF / Download packet. |\n| **Household & income** | The taxpayer, dependents and income sources. |\n| **Preparer tasks** | A checklist for preparing the return; the count shows tasks left. Ticked tasks are remembered in that browser. |\n| **Due-diligence traps** | Only when the scenario has them: planted issues a careful preparer should catch. |\n| **Answer key** | The correct Form 1040 lines. **Locked for preparers** until every preparer task is ticked (lock icon, a notice with progress, then an \"unlocked\" notice). Office and admin accounts always see it. |\n| **Check my return** · Coming soon | Greyed out; can't be opened yet. |\n| **Client interview** · Coming soon | Greyed out; can't be opened yet. |\n\n**Task progress is per browser.** A preparer who switches computer or browser, or clears site data, starts the checklist again (and the answer key locks again until it's done).\n\n## Scenario assistant (AI)\n\nOn **New scenario**, office and admin accounts can describe a client in chat or by voice; the assistant fills the form and generates when the interview is complete. The AI never sets any number in documents or the answer key.\n\n- Up to **120 messages** per conversation and 4,000 characters per message.\n- Messages that look like a real SSN or EIN are refused: use made-up details only.\n- Heavy use is rate-limited for a few minutes.\n\n## PDF downloads\n\nOnly the **admin** can download documents (one document, or the whole packet with a cover sheet). Office accounts and preparers view documents in the browser only; the server refuses downloads for them. Every PDF carries the training watermark.\n\n## Team page and the preparer link\n\nFor office accounts (header → **Team**). An office gives all its preparers one link and one password.\n\n1. Type a password (at least 8 characters) and click **Turn on link**.\n2. Click **Copy link** and send preparers the link and the password.\n\n- **Change password** — preparers already signed in stay signed in; new sign-ins need the new password.\n- **Turn off link** — signs every preparer out; set a password again to turn it back on.\n- Older individual preparer logins (if any) are listed with **Remove access**.\n- Preparers see the office's scenarios and the built-in ones and can't create, save, delete or download.\n\n## Scan & organize (training documents)\n\nPractises the intake step: scan or simulate-scan a scenario's documents, let the reader identify and extract each one, fix what it got wrong, then compare with the answer key.\n\n- It reads **only documents generated by TaxPractice** (stamped TRAINING SAMPLE — NOT FOR FILING). Anything else is refused and nothing from it is kept.\n- Everything runs in the user's browser; nothing is uploaded or stored.\n- Office and admin accounts also see a second tab here, **Check a real return**, which opens the Return checker. Preparers don't see it.\n\n## Return checker (real returns)\n\nOffice and admin accounts only (header → **Return checker**, or Scan & organize → **Check a real return**). It checks a **real, already-prepared 2025 Form 1040** against the client's W-2s and 1099s and against its own arithmetic.\n\n**Private by design.** Everything is read and checked inside the user's browser tab. Nothing is uploaded, saved, logged or sent to AI, and it's gone when the tab closes or the user clicks **Clear**.\n\n### How to use it\n\n1. **Read the 1040 (optional):** pick the PDF saved from the tax software, a scanned PDF, or photos of pages 1 and 2 (upright, page filling the photo). Or type the lines by hand.\n2. **Confirm what was read:** each value sits next to an image of its box. Correct misreadings; leave real mistakes on the return as they are. Values marked **unsure**, and every scanned SSN, are confirmed one by one; the rest with one button. Then **Use these values**.\n3. **Source documents:** **Read W-2s and 1099s from files** (official IRS layouts of W-2, 1099-INT, 1099-DIV, 1099-NEC, 1099-R; several per page is fine; repeat copies are left out), confirm, **Add these documents**. Type anything else (SSA-1099, payroll-company or brokerage layouts).\n4. Set the filing status and boxes (65+, blind, itemizes, Schedule D…) and click **Run checks**.\n\n### What the results mean\n\n- **Boxes filled in wrongly** — format problems: numbers in a name or city, an SSN with letters or the wrong number of digits, an impossible SSN/ITIN, the same SSN twice, a bad state code or ZIP, text or a negative in an amount box, spouse boxes that don't fit the filing status, a half-filled dependent. SSNs are shown masked.\n- **Line checks** — **✓ Agrees**, **✗ Differs** (with the expected amount and the rule), or **? Not checked** (with the reason). Differences of $1 or less count as rounding.\n- It checks: lines from the documents (1a, 2a, 2b, 3a, 3b, 4b, 5b, 6a, 7a, 25a, 25b, 1099-NEC vs Schedule C), the 1040's arithmetic, the standard deduction and the tax on line 16.\n- Not checked yet: 6b, 13a, 13b, 19, 27a, 28 (shown as \"not checked\" when filled in).\n\n**It never says a return is correct.** It is a review aid. Lines it can't verify are always marked \"not checked\", never \"agrees\".\n\n## Admin page\n\nAdmin only (header → **Admin**).\n\n- **Import offices** — paste a list (office name, email, optional phone, e.g. from a spreadsheet). A preview marks rows with no email, repeated emails and the admin's own login before anything is created. Option to give each office its own generated password (shown once).\n- **Offices** — add an office; delete an office (also deletes its scenarios and removes its people's access).\n- **Logins** — add a login (email, password, role, office); change role or office; **Reset password**; edit **Phone**; **Remove access** (removes access to this app only — the login itself stays, because some logins are shared with Referral Circle).\n- Each office's shared preparer login appears as **Preparer link (shared)**.\n- An email that already has a login (e.g. from Referral Circle) is given access with its **existing** password; the password typed in Admin doesn't apply to it.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\nGrouped by what the user sees. Quoted text is the exact on-screen message.\n\n**\"Invalid login credentials\" on Sign in**\n- Cause: Wrong email or password, or the login existed before (Referral Circle) and keeps that app's password, or it signs in with Google only.\n- Fix: Check the email for typos and extra spaces. Ask them to try their Referral Circle password if they have one. Otherwise escalate to the administrator to **Reset password**. Never ask for their current password.\n\n**\"This login has no access to the training site. Ask your administrator to add you to an office.\"**\n- Cause: The email has a login (often from Referral Circle) but no access to TaxPractice, or access was removed.\n- Fix: Escalate to the administrator to add the login to the right office (Admin → Add login or Import offices).\n\n**Preparer link: \"Wrong password, or this office's link is turned off.\"**\n- Cause: Old password (the office changed it) or the office turned the link off.\n- Fix: The preparer asks their office for the current password. The office can check or reset it on the Team page.\n\n**Preparer link: \"Link not recognized\"**\n- Cause: The link was cut off when copied.\n- Fix: Ask the office to send the link again using **Copy link**.\n\n**\"Application error: a client-side exception has occurred\", or the page looks out of date**\n- Cause: Usually a tab left open while a new version went live.\n- Fix: Reload fully: **Ctrl+Shift+R** (Windows) or **Cmd+Shift+R** (Mac), or close the tab and open the site again. If it persists, collect a screenshot, the page address and the first red line from the browser console (F12 → Console) and escalate.\n\n**\"The answer key is locked\"**\n- Cause: By design for preparers: every preparer task must be ticked first. Progress is stored per browser.\n- Fix: Open **Preparer tasks** and tick every task. If they changed computer or browser, they need to tick them again there.\n\n**A scenario disappeared after a reload**\n- Cause: An office account generated it but didn't click **Save scenario**.\n- Fix: It can't be recovered; generate it again (the same template and seed recreate it exactly) and click Save.\n\n**\"… wasn't saved and will be gone after a reload\" / \"wasn't added to the built-in scenarios\"**\n- Cause: The save didn't reach the server (connection, or the account's access changed).\n- Fix: Click **Save scenario** / **Save as built-in** again. If it keeps failing, escalate with the full message.\n\n**\"Still loading your account. Try again in a moment.\" or the button says \"Loading your account…\"**\n- Cause: The page opened a second ago and hasn't finished checking who is signed in.\n- Fix: Wait a moment; the button enables itself.\n\n**\"I can't find New scenario / Delete / Download / Team / Return checker\"**\n- Cause: The account type doesn't include it (see Account types). Downloads are admin-only; preparers can't create or delete.\n- Fix: Explain the role's access. Role changes are made by the administrator.\n\n**\"Your login isn't linked to an office yet\"**\n- Fix: Escalate to the administrator to place the login in an office.\n\n**Scan & organize: \"This page wasn't processed (no TRAINING SAMPLE marking)\"**\n- Cause: By design: the training scanner reads only documents generated by TaxPractice.\n- Fix: Use a scenario's own documents. To check a real return, an office or admin uses the Return checker.\n\n**Return checker: \"This doesn't look like a 2025 Form 1040.\"**\n- Cause: Wrong form or year, a tilted or cropped photo, or a very low-resolution scan.\n- Fix: Use the PDF saved from the tax software, or upright scans of pages 1 and 2 at 200–300 DPI with the page filling the image. Or type the lines by hand.\n\n**Return checker: \"No official-layout W-2 or 1099 was found.\"**\n- Cause: The document isn't in the official IRS layout (payroll-company W-2, brokerage composite 1099) or is an SSA-1099.\n- Fix: Type those amounts with **+ Add W-2** / **+ Add 1099-…**.\n\n**Return checker: many values marked \"unsure\"**\n- Cause: Blurry, dark or tilted pages. Scanned SSNs are always marked unsure because the form's printed dividers can cut through digits.\n- Fix: Compare each with its image and correct it, or rescan flat and upright at 300 DPI.\n\n**\"These amounts aren't numbers: …\"**\n- Fix: If the return really shows that, it's also listed under \"boxes filled in wrongly\". Type the intended number to run the math checks.\n\n**\"A conversation needs 1–120 messages.\"**\n- Fix: Start a new conversation with the assistant (Start over).\n\n**\"Too many requests. Wait a few minutes and try again.\"**\n- Fix: Wait about 10 minutes before using the assistant again.\n\n**\"The AI couldn't answer just now.\" / \"The AI assistant isn't configured\"**\n- Fix: Try again in a moment, or fill the form by hand (templates work without AI). If it persists, escalate.\n\n**\"That message contains what looks like a real SSN or EIN\"**\n- Fix: By design. Remove real identifiers; describe the client with made-up details only.\n\n## Ready-to-send replies\n\n**Can't sign in:** Thanks for reaching out. Please check that you're using the exact email your office login was created with, and that there are no spaces before or after it. If it still says \"Invalid login credentials\", reply to this ticket and we'll have the administrator reset your password and send you a new one. Please don't send us your password.\n\n**Answer key locked (preparer):** The answer key opens once every item on the Preparer tasks tab is ticked. Your progress is saved in the browser you used, so if you switched computer or browser you'll need to tick the tasks again there.\n\n**Page error / old version:** A new version of the site went live while your page was open. Please press Ctrl+Shift+R (Cmd+Shift+R on a Mac) to reload it fully, or close the tab and open the site again.\n\n**Downloads (office):** Documents can be viewed in the browser on the Documents tab. Downloading them as PDFs is limited to the administrator.\n\n**Is my data private? (Return checker):** The Return checker reads and checks everything inside your own browser tab. Nothing is uploaded, saved, logged or sent to AI, and it's cleared when you close the tab or click Clear.\n\n## Privacy and safety answers\n\n- **Training scenarios contain no real people.** Names, employers and identifiers are fictional; SSNs are deliberately in ranges that can't belong to anyone. Every page says TRAINING SAMPLE — NOT FOR FILING.\n- **Training documents can't be filed.** They are watermarked and refused by the app's own scanner if they aren't TaxPractice documents.\n- **The Return checker keeps real data in the browser.** No upload, storage, logging or AI. Offices using it remain responsible for their own taxpayer-data obligations.\n- **Offices are separated.** An office can't see or delete another office's scenarios; this is enforced by the database, not just the screens.\n- **AI never sets numbers.** All amounts and answer keys come from the tax calculator.\n\n## Escalation and ticket intake\n\n### Collect in every ticket\n\n- The login email and office name (never the password).\n- Account type (admin, office, preparer link).\n- The page address and what they clicked, with the time it happened.\n- The exact message on screen, ideally a screenshot. For page errors, the first red line from F12 → Console.\n- Browser and device. For checker reading problems: PDF from software, scan or photo.\n\n**Never collect** passwords, real taxpayer documents, real SSNs or client information. If a user attaches a real tax document to a ticket, delete the attachment and remind them that support never needs client documents.\n\n### Escalate to the administrator\n\n- Password resets, new logins, role or office changes, removing access, offices to add or delete.\n- A scenario that won't save after retrying, or a repeating page error after a full reload.\n- Anything suggesting someone sees another office's scenarios (treat as urgent).\n- Return checker results a user believes are wrong after confirming every value (include the line, the rule shown, expected and found — no client documents).\n\n### Not support's to change\n\n- Who can download, create or delete (set by account type).\n- The answer-key lock for preparers and the \"Coming soon\" tabs.\n- The training scanner refusing non-TaxPractice documents.\n\n## Glossary\n\n| Term | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Scenario** | One fictional client with documents, tasks and an answer key. |\n| **Built-in scenario** | Made by the admin (or bundled); every office and preparer sees it. |\n| **Office scenario** | Made and saved by an office; only that office sees it. |\n| **Seed** | The code that, with the same setup, recreates a scenario exactly. |\n| **Answer key** | The correct Form 1040 lines for a scenario, from the tax calculator. |\n| **Due-diligence trap** | A planted issue in a scenario that a careful preparer should catch. |\n| **Preparer link** | An office's single sign-in link plus password for all its preparers. |\n| **Return checker** | The office/admin tool that checks a real prepared 1040 in the browser. |\n| **Unsure** | A value the checker read but isn't confident about; it must be confirmed on its own. |\n| **Referral Circle** | The owner's other app; some logins are shared with it. |\n";

export const CONTRACT_KB = "# Higher View Contract Workspace: Chatbot Knowledge Base\n\n---\n\n## 0. Instructions for the chatbot\n\n**Who you help**\n- **Owners**: business owners (mostly tax offices) who were invited to use the Contract Workspace. They set up contracts and send them to their clients to sign.\n- **Clients (signers)**: people who received a signing link from an owner.\n- **Admins**: Higher View staff. Admin topics are in Section 9. Only discuss them if the person says they are Higher View staff.\n\n**How to answer**\n- Use simple, friendly, non-technical language. Many users are not tech-savvy.\n- Give step-by-step instructions using the exact button names in **bold**, as they appear on screen.\n- Keep answers short. Answer the question asked, then offer one helpful next step if it fits.\n- If a question is not covered here, do not guess. Say you're not sure and direct them to support: **open a ticket or talk to an agent right here in this support chat**.\n\n**Never do these**\n- Never ask for, repeat, or guess a password. Never ask for card numbers or other sensitive details in chat.\n- Never give legal or tax advice about what a contract means or whether it's enforceable. Say: \"I can help you use the app, but for questions about the contract terms, please talk to your attorney or Higher View support.\"\n- Never promise that a signed contract can be changed. Signed contracts are locked (see 7.4).\n\n---\n\n## 1. What the app is\n\nThe Contract Workspace lets a business owner:\n1. Brand ready-made contracts with their own logo, business name, details, and signature.\n2. Upload their own contracts (PDF) and mark where the client should type, date, and sign.\n3. Send a unique signing link to each client.\n4. Track who has opened and signed, countersign, and download signed PDFs.\n\nClients sign online from any device. **They don't need an account or a password.**\n\n**Key words**\n| Term | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| Owner / Workspace | The business owner and their private online area |\n| Template | A contract set up with the owner's details, ready to send |\n| Signing link | A unique web link for one client to fill in and sign one contract |\n| Countersign | The owner signs after the client has signed |\n| Field | A box on a contract where someone types, dates, signs, or ticks |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Getting access (owners)\n\n### 2.1 The invitation email\nOwners receive an email saying Higher View is sharing a contract template with them. It contains:\n- A gold button: **Open Contract Template**. This opens the owner's private workspace.\n- **Document password**, shown under the button. It's needed to unlock the workspace.\n- A backup link at the bottom (\"If the button doesn't work, copy and paste this link into your browser\").\n\n### 2.2 Opening the workspace\n1. Click **Open Contract Template** in the email (or paste the backup link into a browser).\n2. A box titled **Protected link** appears.\n3. Type or paste the password from the email into the **Password** box.\n4. Click **Unlock** (or press **Enter**).\n\n**Tips**\n- The password shows as dots while typing. That's normal.\n- The workspace **does not remember the password**. Enter it every visit. Bookmark the page and keep the email.\n- The same link and password work every time.\n\n### 2.3 Access problems\n| Problem | What to do |\n|---|---|\n| \"Incorrect password\" | Check for typos, extra spaces at the start or end, and Caps Lock. Copy and paste the password from the email. |\n| Forgot or lost the password | Find the original invitation email (search the inbox and spam for \"Higher View\"). If it's gone, contact support. Support cannot read the password back to you, because it's stored securely. |\n| \"Link not valid: This invitation link is invalid or has been removed.\" | The link was copied incompletely, or the workspace was removed. Re-copy the full link from the email. If it still fails, contact support. |\n| Invitation email never arrived | Check spam/junk and promotions. Then contact support. |\n| Page stuck on \"Loading workspace…\" | Wait a moment and refresh. Try another browser (Chrome, Edge, Safari). If it continues, contact support. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. The workspace layout\n\n- **Top left:** the owner's logo and business name. **Remove logo** appears next to the logo.\n- **Top right:** a status label. **Set up your templates** means setup isn't finished. **Template saved** means at least one contract is ready.\n- **Three tabs:**\n  1. **Customize Templates**: set up the ready-made contracts.\n  2. **My Contracts**: upload your own PDF contracts.\n  3. **Sent Documents**: send contracts and track them.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Customize Templates (ready-made contracts)\n\n### 4.1 Pick a contract\nAt the top, use **Choose a contract to customize**. Only contracts enabled for the owner's account are listed. Possible contracts:\n- **Independent Contractor Agreement**\n- **Service Agreement**\n- **Package Summary & Payment Plan**\n- **Owner Participation Agreement**\n\nA label shows **Not saved yet** or **Saved**. Each contract is saved separately. A contract must be **saved** before it can be sent.\n\n*If an owner expects a contract that isn't in the list, it hasn't been enabled for their account. Contact support.*\n\n### 4.2 Branding & details (left panel)\n\n**Logo (shared across all contracts)**\n- Click **Upload logo** (or **Change logo**), choose an image, and click **Open**.\n- Image files only (PNG, JPG, and similar). Large images are resized automatically.\n- The logo **saves immediately**. There's no need to press Save.\n- It appears on the ready-made contracts and in the workspace header.\n- Remove it with **Remove** (in the panel) or **Remove logo** (top of page).\n- Uploaded contracts (My Contracts) **keep their own letterhead**. The logo doesn't change them.\n\n**Business name (shared)**: shown on every ready-made contract.\n\n**Hero title / Hero subtitle**: the heading and short message the client sees at the top of the signing page. These are pre-filled and can be changed.\n\n**Contract details**: the boxes differ by contract:\n| Contract | Detail boxes |\n|---|---|\n| Independent Contractor Agreement | Company name (Entity Name), Business address, City/State/Zip, Governing law state, Term length (1, 2, or 3 years) |\n| Service Agreement | Company name (Entity Name), Street or business address, City/State/Zip |\n| Package Summary & Payment Plan | Company name, Provider name, Beginners package price, Professional package price |\n| Owner Participation Agreement | Company name (Entity Name), Business address, City/State/Zip, Owner split option (70/30, 80/20, or 50/50 Partnership) |\n\nAnything entered here is filled into every contract sent from this template.\n\n**Your signature (auto-applied to this contract)**\n1. Click **Add signature**. The **Create signature** window opens.\n2. Choose one:\n   - **Draw**: sign with a mouse or finger. **Clear** starts over.\n   - **Type**: type your name and choose a style (Style 1–3).\n   - **Upload**: use a picture of your signature.\n3. Click **Create**. (**Cancel** closes without saving.)\n4. To redo it, click **Change signature**. To delete it, click **Remove**.\n\nThe signature is placed automatically on every copy of that contract.\n\n**Save**: click the green **Save [contract name]** button at the bottom. A green **Template saved** message confirms it, and the label changes to **Saved**.\n\n### 4.3 Preview & fill the template (right panel)\n- Shows exactly what the client will see.\n- You can click blanks inside the contract and fill them in. These values are saved and reused for every contract sent from this template.\n- **Edit**: turn on to change the contract's wording, or which fields are required.\n- **Undo**: reverses the last change.\n- **Save**: saves the edits.\n\n### 4.4 Owner Participation Agreement: payment section\n- Card type is a dropdown: **Visa, Mastercard, AMEX, Discover**.\n- The **Backend** button hides the card fields. It records that the owner will pay the backend fee instead of giving card details. The fee was set at $315.95 when this was written; confirm the current amount with support before quoting it. The owner can switch back to entering a card.\n\n---\n\n## 5. My Contracts (upload your own contract)\n\n### 5.1 Upload\n1. Open the **My Contracts** tab (page title: **Your uploaded contracts**).\n2. Click **Upload contract**.\n3. Choose a **PDF** file and click **Open**.\n\n**PDF only.** For a Word document: in Word, click **File**, then **Save As**, choose **PDF**, then upload that file.\n\nEach uploaded contract shows its name, number of pages, upload date, a **Place fields** button, and a red trash can (delete).\n\nThe signed copy of an uploaded contract is **the original PDF with the answers added**.\n\n### 5.2 Place fields\n1. Click **Place fields**. The contract opens on the left, and the **Field to place** panel is on the right.\n2. Choose a field type:\n   - **Text**: typed answers (name, address, email, etc.)\n   - **Date**\n   - **Signature**\n   - **Checkbox**\n   - **Logo**\n3. On the page, **click, hold, and drag** to draw a box over the blank line, then let go.\n4. Repeat for every blank. Scroll down to reach every page.\n5. Click a placed box to edit its settings. With nothing selected, the panel says \"No field selected.\"\n6. Click **Save layout**. **Required, or the boxes are lost.**\n7. Click **Back** to return to the list.\n\n**Box colors show who fills each box:**\n| Color | Who fills it | When |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Blue** | The client (signer) | When signing |\n| **Violet / purple** | The owner | Before sending |\n| **Amber / orange** | The owner | After the client signs (countersign) |\n\nA counter under the title, for example \"20 placed, 9 for the signer\", shows how many boxes there are and how many are for the client.\n\n**Tips for good alignment**\n- Draw each box right on top of the blank line, about the height of one line of text.\n- Make the box wide enough for the longest expected answer.\n- Check every page before saving.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Sent Documents (sending and tracking)\n\n### 6.1 Send a contract\n1. Open **Sent Documents** (page title: **Your sent agreements**).\n2. Click **New signing link**.\n   - If the button is greyed out, no contract has been saved yet. Save one first.\n3. In **Send a contract**, choose the **Contract**. Both ready-made and uploaded contracts are listed.\n   - \"(save first)\" next to a contract means it isn't saved or set up yet.\n4. Enter **Client name** (optional), **Client email**, and **Client phone**.\n5. Click **Generate link**.\n6. Click the copy button next to the link (\"Link copied\"), then click **Done**.\n7. Paste the link into a text, email, or chat to the client.\n\nEvery client gets their **own unique link**. Create a new link for each client and each contract.\n\n### 6.2 Reading the list\nEach row shows the client's name, the contract name, email, and dates: sent, **Opened** (when the client first opened it), and **Client signed**.\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Pending** | Sent; the client hasn't signed yet |\n| **Awaiting your signature** (orange) | The client signed; the owner needs to **Countersign** |\n| **Signed** | Complete |\n\n### 6.3 Row buttons\n| Button | What it does |\n|---|---|\n| **Copy** | Copies the client's signing link again |\n| **Open** | Opens the contract in a new tab |\n| **Countersign** | Appears when awaiting your signature. Opens the contract so you can fill your amber fields and sign. |\n| **Follow up** | Sends the client a reminder to sign |\n| **Email** | Opens your email app with a ready-made message containing the link |\n| **PDF** | Downloads the signed contract (only after signing) |\n| Red trash can | Deletes the document. **This cannot be undone**, and the client's link stops working. |\n\n---\n\n## 7. The client's side (signing)\n\n### 7.1 Signing steps\n1. Open the link from the owner. No account or password is needed.\n2. The page shows the owner's logo and business name, the label **Secure signing**, and the message \"Please review the agreement below, fill in the highlighted fields, then type your name to sign at the bottom.\"\n3. A guide bar at the bottom shows **START (number of fields)**. Click it to jump to each empty field. A **Fill In** or **Sign** tag points at the current field. Use **Next**, the back arrow, and **Done** to move through.\n4. Fields the owner already filled in are locked. The client can't change them.\n5. Dates such as the agreement date are filled in automatically with today's date.\n6. Signature fields open the **Create signature** window (Draw, Type, or Upload, then **Create**).\n7. At the bottom, under **Sign this agreement**:\n   - Type your full legal name in **Type your full legal name as your signature**.\n   - Tick the box agreeing to the terms. This confirms the typed name is your legal electronic signature.\n   - Click **Sign & Submit**.\n8. \"Agreement signed successfully!\" appears.\n\n### 7.2 After signing\nThe page shows \"This agreement has been signed. Signed by [name] on [date/time].\" and a **Download PDF** button. The client can return to the same link anytime to download it again.\n\n### 7.3 Client problems\n| Problem | What to do |\n|---|---|\n| \"Please type your full name to sign and agree to the terms.\" | Type your full name (at least 2 letters) and tick the agreement box. |\n| **Sign & Submit** is greyed out | The name box is empty or the agreement box isn't ticked. |\n| \"Link not valid: This signing link is invalid or has been removed.\" | The link is incomplete or the owner deleted it. Ask the owner for a new link. |\n| \"This document has already been signed.\" | It was already submitted. Open the link to download the PDF. |\n| \"Could not generate PDF\" | Refresh the page and try again, or try another browser. |\n| Can't draw a signature on a phone | Use **Type** or **Upload** instead. |\n\n### 7.4 Changes after signing\n**Signed contracts are locked and cannot be edited.** This protects the legal record. If something is wrong, the owner should send a **new** signing link with the corrected details.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Frequently asked questions\n\n**Owners**\n\n**Q: How do I log in?**\nClick **Open Contract Template** in your invitation email, enter the **Document password** from the same email, and click **Unlock**.\n\n**Q: Why do I have to type my password every time?**\nFor security, the workspace doesn't remember it. Bookmark the page and keep the email handy.\n\n**Q: Do I need to save after uploading my logo?**\nNo. The logo saves as soon as you pick it.\n\n**Q: Why can't I click \"New signing link\"?**\nYou haven't saved a contract yet. Go to **Customize Templates**, fill in your details, and click **Save**.\n\n**Q: A contract says \"(save first)\".**\nOpen that contract in **Customize Templates** and click **Save**. For an uploaded contract, place the fields and click **Save layout**.\n\n**Q: Can I use my own contract?**\nYes. Go to **My Contracts**, click **Upload contract**, choose a PDF, then use **Place fields** and **Save layout**.\n\n**Q: My contract is a Word file.**\nSave it as PDF first (**File**, then **Save As**, then **PDF**), then upload it.\n\n**Q: Does my logo appear on my uploaded contract?**\nNo. Uploaded contracts keep their own letterhead. You can add a **Logo** field with **Place fields** if you want one.\n\n**Q: What do the blue, violet, and amber boxes mean?**\nBlue: your client fills it in. Violet: you fill it in before sending. Amber: you fill it in after the client signs.\n\n**Q: How do I send a contract?**\n**Sent Documents**, then **New signing link**, choose the contract, enter the client's details, click **Generate link**, copy it, and send it to your client.\n\n**Q: Can I send the same link to two clients?**\nNo. Each client needs their own link. Generate a new one per client.\n\n**Q: How do I know if my client signed?**\nCheck **Sent Documents**. **Awaiting your signature** means they signed and you need to countersign. **Signed** means it's complete. You can also see when they opened it.\n\n**Q: What does \"Awaiting your signature\" mean?**\nYour client signed. Click **Countersign** to add your signature and finish.\n\n**Q: My client hasn't signed.**\nUse **Follow up** to send a reminder, or **Copy** the link and send it again.\n\n**Q: How do I get a copy of the signed contract?**\nClick **PDF** on the signed contract in **Sent Documents**.\n\n**Q: Can I edit a contract after it's signed?**\nNo. Signed contracts are locked. Send a new link with the corrected details.\n\n**Q: I deleted a contract by mistake.**\nDeleting can't be undone, and the old link no longer works. Create a new signing link.\n\n**Q: Can I change which contracts I have access to?**\nContact support. Higher View chooses which contracts are enabled for each account.\n\n**Q: Can I change my password?**\nContact support.\n\n**Clients**\n\n**Q: Do I need an account?**\nNo. Just open the link you received.\n\n**Q: How do I sign?**\nClick **START** at the bottom, fill each highlighted field, then type your full legal name, tick the agreement box, and click **Sign & Submit**.\n\n**Q: Can I sign on my phone?**\nYes. If drawing is hard, use **Type** or **Upload** for your signature.\n\n**Q: Some fields are locked.**\nThose were filled in by the business and can't be changed. Contact the business if something is wrong.\n\n**Q: I made a mistake after signing.**\nSigned contracts can't be edited. Ask the business to send you a new link.\n\n**Q: How do I get my copy?**\nOpen your signing link again and click **Download PDF**.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Admin (Higher View staff only)\n\nAdmins log in with an email and password on the sign-in page. Only accounts with the admin role can use the admin area. Others see \"Admin access required\".\n\n**Admin tabs** include **Sent Documents**, **Owners**, and **Templates**.\n\n**Invite an owner** (**Owners** tab, then **Invite owner**):\n1. Fill in **Full name** (required), **Email**, **Phone**, and **Link password** (required). The owner must enter this password to open their link.\n2. Under **Contracts this owner can use**, tick the contracts to enable. If none are ticked, all contracts are enabled.\n3. Click **Generate invite link**.\n4. The owner's details and link are sent to the CRM (GoHighLevel), which sends the invitation email.\n\n**Notes**\n- Passwords are stored securely (hashed). Nobody can read an existing password back. If an owner loses theirs, a new one must be set.\n- Deleting an owner also deletes their documents and saved templates. It **cannot be undone**. An owner who has prospects can't be deleted until those are handled.\n- Avoid creating the same owner twice. Check the **Owners** list for the email first.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Quick reference\n\n| I want to… | Go to | Click |\n|---|---|---|\n| Unlock my workspace | Invitation email | **Open Contract Template**, then the password, then **Unlock** |\n| Add my logo | Customize Templates | **Upload logo** |\n| Add my signature | Customize Templates | **Add signature**, then **Create** |\n| Save a contract | Customize Templates | **Save [contract]** |\n| Change contract wording | Customize Templates, preview panel | **Edit**, then **Save** |\n| Upload my own PDF | My Contracts | **Upload contract** |\n| Mark signing spots | My Contracts | **Place fields**, then **Save layout** |\n| Send to a client | Sent Documents | **New signing link**, then **Generate link** |\n| Remind a client | Sent Documents | **Follow up** |\n| Sign after the client | Sent Documents | **Countersign** |\n| Download a signed copy | Sent Documents | **PDF** |\n";

/** Handbooks plus the rules for using them, appended to the support-chat system prompt. */
export function knowledgeBlock(): string {
  return [
    "=== TAXPRACTICE APP SUPPORT HANDBOOK ===",
    "Higher View also runs TaxPractice, a training simulator for tax preparers. When a customer asks about TaxPractice (signing in, scenarios, the answer key, preparer links, Scan & organize, the Return checker, the Admin or Team page, or any TaxPractice error message), answer only from the handbook below. Quote exact on-screen messages and button names. If the handbook doesn't cover it, say so and offer to open a ticket.",
    "Rules: never ask for a password, real SSNs, or client documents (only the login email and office name). When the handbook says to escalate to the administrator (password resets, new logins, role or office changes, a scenario that won't save after retrying, a repeating page error, or anyone seeing another office's scenarios), call create_ticket with the details collected. Treat a report of seeing another office's scenarios as the highest priority.",
    "",
    TAXPRACTICE_KB,
    "",
    "=== CONTRACT WORKSPACE SUPPORT HANDBOOK ===",
    "Higher View also runs the Contract Workspace, where business owners brand or upload contracts and send signing links to their clients. When someone asks about it (the invitation email, the document password, Unlock, Customize Templates, My Contracts, Place fields, Sent Documents, signing links, countersigning, signed PDFs, or any Contract Workspace error message), answer only from the handbook below and follow its section 0 instructions. Use the exact button names. If the handbook doesn't cover it, say you're not sure and offer to open a ticket or connect them with an agent.",
    "Rules: never ask for, repeat, or guess a password, and never ask for card numbers. Support can't read a password back; a lost password or link, a missing invitation email, changing contracts or passwords, or a page that keeps failing means call create_ticket with the details collected. Wherever the handbook says \"contact support\", that means this chat: offer create_ticket or request_human_agent. Give no legal or tax advice about contract terms, and never promise a signed contract can be changed. Only discuss section 9 (Admin) if the person says they are Higher View staff.",
    "",
    CONTRACT_KB,
  ].join("\n");
}
